{"id": "EUVD-2026-72356", "enisaUuid": "b579802b-6915-3e4b-89a9-f2edf13570f3", "description": "A flaw was found in FreeIPA. The self-managed OTP token ACI does not require authentication and does not restrict which attributes may be added alongside the token entry. An unauthenticated LDAP client can exploit this, combined with a related flaw in the underlying directory server's ACI evaluation (tracked separately), to create an arbitrary attacker-controlled Kerberos principal and have it added to the administrators group. This allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to obtain genuine FreeIPA administrator-group membership and perform administrative operations against the directory and, on SID-enabled deployments, other IdM services.", "datePublished": "2026-09-07T12:01:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T05:08:10", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:70564", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:72279", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:82935", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83083", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83084", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83085", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83460", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83461", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-76578", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2519522"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cgrx-2q4j-9f37", "CVE-2026-76578"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 1.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "004e8323-7fd7-31e4-a4c6-ca8bbd5b299f", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8.8 Update Services for SAP Solutions", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 8080020261007071832.b0a6ceea"}, {"id": "0822ba18-47c6-3733-ad46-f70ce357e2b2", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.2 Update Services for SAP Solutions", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "pa